Miracast through a V4L2 hardware H.264 encoder (v4l2h264enc).

GNOME Network Displays knows x264, openh264 and VA-API encoders only; on a
phone SoC without VA-API (the Pro¹x's Venus) it encoded 1080p in software
with x264, too slow for a smooth picture.  v4l2h264enc is tried first, in
baseline, at a constant bit rate whose peak is the rate itself; its
controls are set before the device opens, since Venus's firmware died when
they changed on a running encoder.  For fxtec-pro1x-guix (AGPL-3.0-or-later);
the program's own licence (GPL-3.0-or-later) applies to this change upstream.

